# API Integration Rules

Rules for all Gemini API interactions. Reference [src/extension/background.js](mdc:src/extension/background.js) for implementation.

## API Endpoint

- Base URL: `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/`
- Primary Model: `gemini-2.0-flash:generateContent`
- Fallback Model: `gemini-1.5-flash:generateContent`
- Rate Limits: 15 req/min, 1500/day (free tier)

## Request Format

```javascript
{
  contents: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      parts: [{ text: prompt }]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Response Parsing

```javascript
const text = response.data.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text;
```

## Retry Logic

Implemented in [src/extension/background.js](mdc:src/extension/background.js):

- Exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s max
- Max attempts: 3
- Jitter: 25% random variation
- Retry on: 503, 500, UNAVAILABLE
- Don't retry on: 429 (rate limit)

## Rate Limit Handling

```javascript
if (response.status === 429 || isResourceExhausted) {
  return {
    success: false,
    error: friendlyMessage,
    rateLimited: true,
    retryAfter: 60000 // ms
  };
}
```

## Caching Strategy

### Analysis Cache
- Location: [src/extension/modules/twitter.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/twitter.js)
- TTL: 30 minutes
- Key: Content hash + analysis type

### Validation Cache
- Location: [src/extension/modules/validation.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/validation.js)
- TTL: 5 minutes
- Key: API key hash

## Request Optimization

- Request scheduler: Prevent duplicate concurrent calls
- Image prompts: Manual only (not automatic)
- Batch operations: Group related requests
- Cache hits: Reuse cached analysis when possible

## Error Messages

- User-friendly: No technical jargon
- Actionable: Tell user what to do
- No data leakage: Don't expose API keys or internal details

## Fallback Model

If primary model fails:
1. Try fallback model on last retry attempt
2. Log model switch for debugging
3. User sees same interface (transparent fallback)

## Security

- API keys stored in Chrome Storage Local (encrypted)
- Never log API keys
- Don't expose keys in error messages
- Validate keys before saving
